From 0000000000000000000000000000000000009004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MinsOS <minsos@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] IProcessObserver tolerates a missing onProcessStarted (One UI 9, y2q)

Settings mod framework.jar 9004-oneui85 (30a4599) re-derived on the S918B
IProcessObserver$Stub. An app built against an older IProcessObserver (Shizuku) has no
5-arg onProcessStarted, so the dispatch throws AbstractMethodError on its binder thread
and the app dies at start. Catch it and return the transaction as handled. One UI 9 uses
v1..v6 for the call and v0 for the result (8.5: v2..v7 and v1), so the handler takes
the exception in v1 and v0 (true) is returned unchanged.
---
--- a/smali/android/app/IProcessObserver$Stub.smali
+++ b/smali/android/app/IProcessObserver$Stub.smali
@@ -263,8 +263,16 @@
 
     move-object v1, p0
 
+    :try_start_ipo
     invoke-virtual/range {v1 .. v6}, Landroid/app/IProcessObserver$Stub;->onProcessStarted(IIILjava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;)V
+    :try_end_ipo
+    .catch Ljava/lang/AbstractMethodError; {:try_start_ipo .. :try_end_ipo} :catch_ipo
 
     :goto_0
     return v0
+
+    :catch_ipo
+    move-exception v1
+
+    goto :goto_0
 .end method
